# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Condition> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'AcademicEligibilityRequirement' captures the universal concept of academic suitability/standing requirements without jurisdiction-specific terms. It is a subclass of cco:Condition and retains only axioms applicable to both aligned classes, satisfying the pattern's constraints on neutrality and universal applicability." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Academic Eligibility Requirement" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicEligibilityRequirementPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A condition that must be satisfied by a student to demonstrate they meet the academic criteria required for enrollment or continuation in an educational program, as determined by the institution." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'AcademicWithdrawalResource' is jurisdiction-neutral, avoids program-specific terminology, and reflects the universal purpose of the classes as resources for recording withdrawal details. It satisfies the pattern's constraints by being a subclass of cco:Resource and ensuring all axioms apply universally across aligned jurisdictions." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Academic Withdrawal Resource" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AcademicWithdrawalResourcePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A resource used to document or confirm a student's withdrawal from a study period, including details such as the date, time, and specific units of study affected by the withdrawal." .
