<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessObligation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An obligation to carry out, manage, and maintain various stages and components of an assessment process, including development, execution, independence, documentation, and alignment." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'AssessmentProcess' is jurisdiction-neutral, avoiding any region-specific terminology while capturing the core concept of procedural evaluation shared by both aligned classes. It maintains compatibility with the cco:Resource supertype and satisfies all pattern constraints by focusing on the universal aspect of assessment procedures across jurisdictions." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assessment Process" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#AssessmentProcessPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A structured procedure for conducting and documenting the evaluation of knowledge, skills, or competencies through standardized methods." .
# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Condition> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'CircumstanceCondition' captures the common element of 'circumstances' across all aligned classes while maintaining jurisdiction neutrality. It is a subclass of cco:Condition as required, and the label/definition avoid jurisdiction-specific terms while reflecting the universal concept of conditions tied to exceptional or changing situations." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Circumstance Condition" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CircumstanceConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A condition arising from specific circumstances that may affect eligibility or require adjustment in program requirements." .
