# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Condition> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'CourseCompletionCondition' combines the universal concepts of 'course completion' (from gro-au:CourseRequirement) and 'condition' (from the CCO supertype). It avoids jurisdiction-specific terms while capturing the shared purpose of both classes as requirements for academic completion. The definition explicitly covers both requirement fulfillment and completion verification across jurisdictions." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Course Completion Condition" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#CourseCompletionConditionPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A condition that must be satisfied for the successful completion of an educational program or study period, encompassing both requirements to be met and verification of completion criteria." .
