# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'LearningPause' is jurisdiction-neutral, combining the universal concepts of 'learning' and 'pause' present in both aligned classes. It avoids jurisdiction-specific terms while accurately reflecting the shared functional equivalence of temporary interruptions in educational engagement across systems." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Learning Pause" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#LearningPausePattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A period during which an individual's learning or study activities are formally paused, typically subject to specific duration limits and exceptions." .
