<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#PostCredentialTrainingPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name 'PostCredentialTraining' combines the concept of training occurring after initial credentialing (from gro-ca:PostCredentialTrainingPeriod) with the general training purpose (from gro-uk:RepeatedTraining and gro-uk:Learning). It avoids jurisdiction-specific terms, maintains compatibility with the cco:Resource hierarchy, and satisfies universal applicability across all aligned classes." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#PostCredentialTrainingPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Post-Credential Training" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto#PostCredentialTrainingPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Training required after obtaining a formal credential to meet the accreditation or licensing requirements of a regulated profession, including repeated training, apprenticeship learning, or structured post-credential development periods." .
