<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/au#GapFee> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A tuition fee for a course includes the maximum amount covered by a VET Student Loan and the remaining tuition cost not covered by the loan – the ‘gap fee’. As it’s part of the tuition fee, the gap fee can’t include fees for non-tuition services such as items and equipment that become the student’s physical property and are not consumed in the course (for example, maps, charts or textbooks)." .
