<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#ParentsContributionFromAssets> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#StudentContributionFromIncome> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A financial contribution from a student, parent, step-parent, sponsor, legal guardian or spouse to assist with the cost of the student’s program of study. The contribution is automatically assessed during the student need assessment process." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00832> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Expected Contribution from Need-Based Bursaries" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The expected contribution from need-based bursaries, where the eligibility criteria are based on need, but the funding is not targeted for a specific element of the costs of living or education. The expected contribution is equivalent to the assessed actual amount, less an exemption of $1,800 per program year for both merit-based scholarships and need-based bursaries combined. Any amount of scholarship/bursary funding above $1,800 is considered income and is assessed at 100%." .
