<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#MutuallyExclusiveCourses> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#MutuallyExclusiveCourses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#MutuallyExclusiveCourses> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mutually Exclusive Courses" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#MutuallyExclusiveCourses> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Courses that have a different course name and number but have the same content as another course. Students who are taking duplicate or mutually exclusive courses will not be granted credit for a second time and the duplicate course will not be counted when determining a student’s course load of study for StudentAid BC purposes." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#MutuallyExclusiveCourses> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00844> .
