<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00380_condition_eligibility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00380_condition_eligibility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00380_condition_eligibility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Condition> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00380_condition_eligibility> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#hasConditionExpression> "A letter from a responsible third party testifying as to the truthfulness of the student’s explanation and providing an independent assessment of the situation. The ‘third party’ could be any of the following: counselor, psychologist, religious advisor, doctor, teacher, and/or mature relative outside the immediate family or family friend (the status of the third party and their relationship to the student must be identified in the letter)." .
