<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_authority_ee7f67> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Condition> .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#hasConditionExpression> "A letter from the parent(s) confirming the irreconcilable breakdown in family relations and their refusal to support the student may be submitted. If the family rift is so serious that a parental letter cannot be obtained, a letter from a professional third party having first-hand knowledge of the situation may be substituted. If the student was a youth under the guardianship or in an agreement with a provincial or territorial child welfare agency on their 19th birthday, relevant documentation confirming their status is required." .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Eligibility Criteria" .
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381_condition_c45601> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00381> .
